{{!-- A1, "Magazine cover": a single lead story at display size, then the latest in a
three-column grid. The designed cover — featured strip, writers row, newsletter band —
arrives with the Feed ticket; the arrangement is what distinguishes it from A2.

Every slot comes from the {{#get}} in home.hbs, sliced by {{#foreach}}'s from/to. Slicing
rather than excluding is deliberate: get.js only optimises a filter carrying exactly one
`id:-` term, so a chain of exclusions turns the most-requested URL on the site into an
uncacheable per-visitor query. Positions cannot collide, so no exclusion is needed. --}}
{{#foreach feed limit="1"}}
	<article class="{{post_class}} border-border mb-12 border-b pb-12">
		{{#primary_tag}}<a href="{{url}}" class="font-meta text-accent text-[12px] uppercase">{{name}}</a>{{/primary_tag}}
		<h2 class="font-display text-display mt-3 leading-none tracking-tight">
			<a href="{{url}}" class="text-text no-underline">{{title}}</a>
		</h2>
		<p class="font-body text-muted text-lead measure mt-4">{{excerpt words="40"}}</p>
		{{> "post-meta" byline=true}}
	</article>
{{/foreach}}

<h2 class="font-meta text-muted mb-6 text-[12px] uppercase">{{t "Latest"}}</h2>

<div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
	{{#foreach feed from="2" to="7" columns="3"}}
		<article class="{{post_class}}">
			<h3 class="font-display text-h4 tracking-tight">
				<a href="{{url}}" class="text-text no-underline">{{title}}</a>
			</h3>
			{{> "post-meta"}}
		</article>
	{{/foreach}}
</div>
